ooding caused by excessive rainfall which occurred over\nthe last couple of days is expected or ongoing.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\nSouthwestern Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will occur in low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 852 AM MDT, flooding was occurring along the Rio Grande River\nin low lying and agricultural areas. This high water is due to\nall of the heavy rain which occurred over the last couple of\ndays.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include low lying\nareas in parts of Alamosa and parts of Conejos counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T09:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.596148dc4b6e7104cce02aa2eaee388cb3f30324.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.596148dc4b6e7104cce02aa2eaee388cb3f30324.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 5:29PM MDT until October 25 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding likely along the Rio Grande between Monte Vista and\nAlamosa.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County and West Central Alamosa\nCounty...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Rio Grande and low lying agricultural\nareas in Rio Grande and Alamosa counties is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 525 PM MDT, Emergency management reports flooding of low lying\nareas along and near the Rio Grande in Rio Grande county and in\nAlamosa county upstream of the city of Alamosa.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties between Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaD